MAX true-N over cores = 36
COMPACTNESS LEMMA (single-perturbation form, PROVEN-modulo-core-bound):
  If S = C u {w} with C a 12-subset of {1..13} and L(S) < 1/1260, then w <= 36.
  Hence min positive L over single perturbations is attained at BOUNDED w,
  and exhaustive search w<=2000 (done) proves it = 1/1260.

THE REMAINING GAP for full inf L>0:
  This argument fixes 12 elements in {1..13}. The general claim needs: ANY
  primitive 13-set with small L is within bounded Hamming distance of a tight
  config (empirically true, hAP<=2 over large search) AND the perturbing
  elements are bounded. The decoupling floor (6/7)meas(G_C) handles ONE large
  element per fixed 12-core; iterating handles k large elements as long as the
  remaining (13-k)-core has positive lonely measure bounded below. Proving a
  UNIFORM positive lower bound on meas(G_C) over ALL 12-subsets C (or showing
  finitely many tight 13-sets) is the open crux.
